Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||09-15-2000||12:16 PM||||That would be waaaaaaaaaaay south of The Hague, since these trucs have Belgium license plates...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But true, gas prices are rediculously high, and 65% of it is taxes.<P>Also, I think your dutch friend is a bit mistaken with the price per liter. One liter of unleaded 95 octane = US$0.96. One US gallon = 3.7854 liter. So that's US$3.64 per gallon.<P>Still, it's more expensive than it has ever been. But it's a bit difficult to express that in dollars since the dollar is very expensive too now. If I recalculate the above to what a dollar was about a year ago, then it would be even more than $5 per gallon.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||09-16-2000||02:30 AM||||Same thing in Australia...I was back there 3 yrs ago. It was .82/liter AUS $. Not sure what it is at the moment...Not a lot of V8's there consequently!<P>Cliff, I thought a U.S. imperial gallon was 3.4 liters approx. Not being picky; just curious about my info. <P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000004||olympic||09-16-2000||03:51 AM||||Cliff is right, a US gallon is  3.78 liters.  An imperial gallon is 4.54 liters.  Thats why Canadians and the English get better mpg, their gallon is bigger!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>    Here's a neat little conversion calculator I found.   <A HREF="http://www.jacksprogramming.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jacksprogramming.com</A> <P>A quick tip for other Canadians here.  To figure your mpg(imperial gallon) from liters and kilometers do this:  km/l * 2.814 = mpg<P>And one more thing.  Gas in my town is at 69.8 cents per liter right now for regular unleaded.  So $0.698 CDN * 0.67(exchange rate) = $0.468 US per liter.  Then multiply by 3.785 to get US gallon.   So it equals $1.77US/gal which is still higher than in the US but not as bad as in Europe.   I read an article a while back that said the prices that gas companies charge are almost identical all over the world.  The price differences from country to country are due solely to taxes.<p>[This message has been edited by olympic (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||1
