Z||000017||Greg Piet||09-17-2000||06:34 AM||||I am in the states, but I use the metric system primarily (especially when at work).  I hate having to convert over from US to metric when talking to people from other countries.<P>Even working on my car I primarily talk about what metric size wrench I need (those metrinch tools make it easier to do this).<P>Yes our clocks are in base 12, and a LOT of other countries use Base 24 for this which avoids confusion am/pm confusion!<P>Also metric is entirely Base 10...   Look at your hands...   there are 10 little things sticking out (I beleive they are called fingers and thumbs)...   Add them up and you get 10.   hmmm    base ten seems to make sense to me.  <P>All this gallon junk is annoying...   especially US gallon or Imperial gallon.<P>then there are pounds which just...   awww heck with it now im getting all fired up!<P>||||reg||1
